This directory note is not read by anything.

/etc/motd is shipped EMPTY on purpose. Debian's stock /etc/motd (286 bytes of
"the exact distribution terms ... ABSOLUTELY NO WARRANTY") is printed by
pam_motd on every serial and SSH login, immediately before our own banner, and
two banners on an 80-column console at 115200 baud is just noise. The dynamic
banner in /etc/update-motd.d/00-omni-banner replaces it.

Debian also ships /etc/update-motd.d/10-uname, which prints the same `uname -a`
line our banner already reports as `kernel`. It is left in place rather than
deleted: it is a distro-owned file, removing it invites a package update to put
it back and look like a regression, and one duplicated line is a smaller problem
than fighting dpkg.
